- op: discuss  # a0ac
  at: '2026-09-17T10:14:45Z'  # a0ac
  by: agent  # a0ac
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a0ac
  clock: 5  # a0ac
  nonce: a0ac  # a0ac
  message: "DONE in PRs #1024 and #1025. VERDICT: recall defect, not correct behavior.\nRe-ran this row's own filed repro (hypergumbo survey <apollo-server> --out F,\nthen analysis_runs[] for the two pass ids) before and after.\n\n                             before              after\n  graphql-linker             29 nodes,  0 edges  29 nodes,  22 edges\n  graphql-resolver-linker    91 nodes,  0 edges  91 nodes, 106 edges\n                            ---------------------------------------\n                            120 nodes,  0 edges  193 nodes, 128 edges\n\nplus graphql-sdl-linker's 73 schema nodes (a new pass; emits no edges by\ndesign). Artifacts: ~/hg_wi_dinum_acceptance/{after,final}.json.\n\nROOT CAUSE, and it is not framework detection (which this row correctly told\nme not to blame). Both linkers take the DESTINATION of every edge they can\nemit from symbols with language == \"graphql\", and the only producer of those\nis the GraphQL ANALYZER, which reads *.graphql / *.gql and nothing else.\nMeasured across the archive: of 794 surveys carrying a GraphQL linker run,\nthe analyzer ran in THREE. apollo-server has ZERO .graphql files and 22 source\nfiles containing `type Query` -- the schema is in `gql` tagged template\nliterals, the dominant idiom in the ecosystem. The framework gate opened, the\nlinkers ran, they read the right files, and their dst side did not exist.\n\nCORPUS-WIDE, NOT JUST HERE:\n  graphql-linker           14 runs, 0 with edges -- it had NEVER emitted one\n  graphql-resolver-linker  794 runs, 2 with edges (the same repo, twice)\n\nAND ONE BRANCH WAS UNREACHABLE BY CONSTRUCTION RATHER THAN BY CIRCUMSTANCE.\ngraphql_resolver's `implements` edge keys on kind=\"field\" carrying\nmeta[\"parent_type\"], and NO producer anywhere in the tree emits a GraphQL\nfield symbol -- the analyzer emits type / input / interface / enum / scalar /\nunion / directive / fragment / operation and never `field`. So schema_lookup\nwas always empty and that branch was dead on every repository ever surveyed.\nIts 100% coverage came from tests that hand-construct the symbol: green in CI,\ndead in production. A consumer keyed to a shape nothing produces is the\ninstrument-with-no-reader defect inverted, and an empty dict yields silently.\n\nTHE FIX, in two parts.\n  #1024 graphql-sdl-linker (new, Infrastructure, priority 55) mints schema\n  type / interface / FIELD symbols from SDL embedded in gql tagged templates.\n  Class A per ADR-0031 (a `type User { ... }` in a gql template is a real\n  declaration in a real language with a real span -- the vue_component and\n  grpc-proto-scan precedents), so both consumers read it through their\n  EXISTING filters unchanged. Only the three kinds a consumer reads are\n  minted: minting input/enum/union nodes nothing can link to would be this\n  row's own defect one level down.\n  #1025 gives graphql-linker the client-to-server join it never had. Its\n  original join matched client operation NAME to schema operation NAME -- but\n  a client operation name is an arbitrary client-side label and a schema does\n  not declare one, so that match only fires when another DOCUMENT declares the\n  same name. `query GetUsers { users { id } }` invokes Query.users, and\n  Query.users is a thing a schema really does declare.\n\nON THE ROW'S OWN QUESTION \"if correct, why are 120 nodes worth minting\": they\nare worth minting, and now they are linkable. The nodes were never the\nproblem; the missing destination was.\n\nTWO THINGS FOUND IN THE BODIES AND FIXED IN #1025, since shipping around them\nwould leave a known-false statement in a file being edited:\n  * confidence=0.9 if call.operation_name else 0.7 sat INSIDE\n    `if call.operation_name:` -- the 0.7 arm was unreachable.\n  * graphql-linker's depends_on named six HOST languages. It reads source\n    files itself and consumes no host analyzer's output. Now\n    [[\"graphql\", \"graphql-sdl-linker\"]] -- the two passes that can supply a\n    destination. (Same too-wide shape as WI-ditir, which this settles for\n    graphql-linker; graphql-resolver-linker's clause is still on that row.)\n\nRESIDUAL, NOT ASSERTED CLOSED: extraction is bounded to gql/graphql tagged\ntemplates and gql() triple-quoted calls. An untagged `const typeDefs = ` +\nbacktick, a schema loaded from a file at runtime, or a multi-line field\nargument list are all unclaimed -- deliberately, because scanning source text\nfor `type X {` was tried and matches every TypeScript `interface ITrace {` and\nprose inside comments (it produced \"types\" named `to`, `is` and `for` on this\nvery repo). Under-reporting by design, in the direction that cannot make a\nfalse positive claim."  # a0ac
